cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CONIFER, please cite it as below."
title: "CONIFER: compositional nonlinear-debiased Fay-Herriot small-area estimation with ellipsoidal conformal regions"
abstract: >-
  CONIFER is a Python package for design-aware small-area estimation of forest
  diameter distributions. It implements a compositional area-level Fay-Herriot
  estimator with a cross-fitted, one-step-debiased machine-learned mean and
  design-aware conformal prediction sets on the simplex, and reduces exactly to
  classical Fay-Herriot when the mean is linear.
type: software
